            <div xml:id="d611">

                <pb facs="0937" n="817" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg817"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A 4e/16: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-07T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 7, 1922—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 7—8:39
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3. I propose Chinese proposal that Shanghai market values for six months, October
                    to April, be taken as the basis new tariff. Arnold.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
